\u2192 none\n- `p.get(\"void_cause\")` \u2192 none\n\nSo a minimal `p = {\"pass_id\": pid}` suffices. Then `f = pfacts.get(pid)`.\n\nBut `pfacts = ci.get(\"passes\") or {}`. For the job, `pfacts = {\"dim1#p1\": {...}}`. So set `passes_src = [{\"pass_id\": pid} for pid in pfacts]` when no \u00a75 record.\n\nThen `f = pfacts[\"dim1#p1\"]` = `{\"evaluator\": \"evaluator\", \"call\": \"dim1#p1\", \"run\": 1, \"batch\": \"b1\", \"failureCondition\": {DIM: \"x\"}, \"evidence\": {DIM: \"verdict-p1.json\"}}`.\n\nThen `dims_read = [DIM]`. `n_passes = 1`. `call = link_call(ev_calls, \"evaluator\", \"dim1#p1\", \"eval_artifact\", ...)`. \n\n`ev_calls[\"evaluator\"]` must be the named calls dict from `evaluator_history`. If `H.read_log` reads the call with name \"dim1#p1\", then `named[\"dim1#p1\"] = call`. Then link_call returns it. Good. Then `H.cross_check(ref, \"passes.dim1#p1.at\", None, call.at, ...)`. cross_check with hand None \u2192 probably no refusal. Then `at_v = H.iso(call.at)`, `xc = {\"call\": call.label, \"at_basis\": call.at_basis}`. `call.source_at()` \u2192 maybe None or something. If it returns a file:line, great. If not, `at_source` absent \u2192 D4 fails.\n\nHmm. So I need `at_source` to contain \"harness-eval.log\". I can override after link_call using the new module:\n\n```python\nif call is not None:\n    ...\n    src = harness_source(log_for_evaluator, f.get(\"call\"))  # \"harness-eval.log:1\"\n    if src: xc[\"at_source\"] = src\n```\n\nBut I need the log path in scope. `evaluator_history` returns `eh` but not the log path. I could add it to the returned dict, e.g. `eh[\"log\"] = log`. But `evaluator_history` returns `{\"calls\":..., \"endpoint\":..., \"x\":...}`. I can add `\"log\": log`.\n\nThen in build, when building a check, I have access to `ev_logs` mapping evaluator id \u2192 log path. Hmm, I'd need to store it. Let me add `ev_log_path[e.get(\"id\")] = eh.get(\"log\")`.\n\nAlternatively, store the file:line source directly on each Call via th