I should ensure the module handles an empty list log: `items=[]`, returns {}. Then `entries={}`. Fine.\n\nAlso, the module handles a dict with no \"call\" (e.g., if the log is a generation reply)? It would raise \"names no call\". But evaluator logs are call logs. Fine.\n\nNow, could `harness_log.read` break on a log that `H.read_log` accepts like a JSON list where some entries are generation objects? No, harness logs are only calls.\n\nLet me finalize the module docstring, ensuring no non-ASCII issues? The repo uses `\u00a7` elsewhere, so UTF-8 is fine. I'll keep ASCII to be safe, except maybe. I'll use plain ASCII.\n\nLet me write the final answer.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the `linkable` logic once more for a subtle bug: `linkable = (f.get(\"call\") in ev_map) if f.get(\"call\") else bool(ev_map)`. For D4 if `H.read_log` returns empty calls, `ev_map` = {} \u2192 `f.get(\"call\")` truthy \u2192 `(\"dim1#p1\" in {})` = False \u2192 skip link_call. Good. Then entry found \u2192 at_v set. Good.\n\nFor D6: evaluator_history returns {} \u2192 ev_calls[\"evaluator\"] = {} \u2192 same as above. But ref already non-empty \u2192 refuse. Good.\n\nFor D11: ev_calls has no \"evaluator\" key \u2192 `ev_calls.get(\"evaluator\")` = None \u2192 `ev_map = {}`. Same. Good.\n\nNow, what if `f.get(\"call\")` is None (custody pass has no call)? Then `linkable = bool(ev_map)`. If ev_map non-empty, link_call with named=None \u2192 tries default \"eval_artifact\" if in calls else if single call. Could refuse. That matches existing behavior for \u00a75 records. Fine.\n\nNow write.\n\nLet me also double check the `else` block indentation: it's inside `if rec:`/`else:`. Yes.\n\nNow the final module content. Let me include a note about accepting a single object.\n\nI'll now produce the blocks."}, "reasoning_content": "Let me understand the task. We have a frozen bar `tests/test_evaluator_harness_log.py` that is red: 12 tests, 2 failures (D4 and D8).\n\nLet me analyze the tests to understand what's needed.\n\nThe tests are in two classes:\n\n1. `HarnessLogShapeTests` (D1-D3): run `or_call.py` with mock transport, assert on the log entry. These pass already presumably.\n\n2. `EmitterReadsTheLogTests` (D4-D11): build a job directory, run `kit/emit_custody.py --job-dir job`, check the record/refusal.\n\nLet me look carefully at `_job()`:\n\n```python\ndef _job(self, log_text, evaluator_kind=\"model\"):\n    job = self.td / \"job\"\n    (job / \"inputs\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    (job / \"custody\" / \"evidence\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    (job / \"custody\" / \"evidence\" / \"harness-eval.log\").write_text(log_text)\n    (job / \"custody\" / \"bar.md\").write_text(\"bar\\n\")\n    bar_sha = hashlib.sha256((job / \"custody\" / \"bar.md\").read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n    ledger = [\n        {\"event\": \"freeze\", \"at\": \"2026-11-08T10:00:00Z\", \"bar_file\": \"custody/bar.md\",\n         \"bar_sha256\": bar_sha, \"writer\": \"test_evaluator_harness_log.py\"},\n        {\"event\": \"approve\", \"role\": \"buyer\", \"by\": \"Steve Moitozo II\", \"kind\": \"person\",\n         \"at\": \"2026-11-08T10:00:01Z\", \"barDigest\": bar_sha, \"adopted\": None,\n         \"writer\": \"test_evaluator_harness_log.py\"},\n    ]\n    (job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\").write_text(\n        \"\".join(json.dumps(e) + \"\\n\" for e in ledger))\n    custody = {\n        \"custody_inputs\": \"plumbline/custody-inputs/v1\",\n        \"orchestrator\": {...},\n        \"bar\": {\"file\": \"custody/bar.md\", \"author\": \"architect\",\n                \"dimensions\": [{\"id\": DIM, \"criterion\": \"x\", \"scale\": {\"type\": \"pass_fail\", \"threshold\": 1}}]},\n        \"evaluators\": [{\"id\": \"evaluator\", \"who\": \"plumbline-eval\", \"name\": \"plumbline-eval\",\n                        \"kind\": evaluator_kind,\n                        \"harness_log\": \"custody/evidence/harness-eval.log\",\n                        \"model\": {\"family\": \"glm\", \"identifier\": \"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\",\n                                  \"endpoint\": \"api.z.ai\", \"readOnly\": True},\n                        \"runs\": 3}],\n        \"passes\": {\"dim1#p1\": {\"evaluator\": \"evaluator\", \"call\": \"dim1#p1\", \"run\": 1,\n                               \"batch\": \"b1\", \"failureCondition\": {DIM: \"x\"},\n                               \"evidence\": {DIM: \"verdict-p1.json\"}}},\n        \"retention\": {\"where\": str(job)},\n        \"disposition\": {\"state\": \"not_yet_given\", \"by\": \"Steve Moitozo II\"},\n    }\n    (job / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").write_text(json.dumps(custody))\n    (job / \"packet.json\").write_text(json.dumps(\n        {\"job_id\": \"harness-log-j\", \"terminal_state\": \"accepted\", \"outcome\": \"accepted\",\n         \"disposition_state\": \"not_yet_given\"}))\n    (job / \"custody\" / \"bar.md\").write_text(\"bar\\n\")\n    return job\n```\n\nSo the job has:\n- `packet.json` with terminal_state accepted\n- `inputs/custody.json` with:\n  - bar: file `custody/bar.md`, author, dimensions `[{\"id\": DIM, ...}]`\n  - evaluators: one evaluator `id: evaluator`, `kind: model` (or \"command\" for D11), harness_log `custody/evidence/harness-eval.log`, model identifier `z-ai/glm-5.3-flash`, endpoint `api.z.ai`, readOnly\n  - passes: `dim1#p1` with evaluator `evaluator`, call `dim1#p1`, run 1, batch `b1`, failureCondition `{DIM: \"x\"}`, evidence `{DIM: \"verdict-p1.json\"}`\n  - retention where job\n  - disposition state `not_yet_given`, by Steve\n- `inputs/custody-events.jsonl` with freeze line (writer test...) and approve buyer line\n- `custody/evidence/harness-eval.log` with log_text\n- No `iteration-*-eval-record.json` \u2014 so `rec` is None. The emitter's `xp[\"verdict\"] = ci.get(\"verdict\")` (None) and gaps.add(\"x-plumbline.verdict\", ...) non-hard.\n\nSo the emitter goes through `build()` normal path (not build_finish since no finish/round records).\n\nNow the spec, for this job, has no \u00a75 record. So `passes_src` is empty, `run` is None. Then checks come only from `ci.get(\"checks\")` which is empty. So 0 checks, gap \"no filed pass and no recorded check\" (hard!). That would exit 1, not 0. Hmm.\n\nWait, D4 wants: `checks` non-empty and the record's check time names the harness log. D4 asserts:\n\n```python\nchecks = (rec.get(\"predicate\") or {}).get(\"checks\") or []\nself.assertTrue(checks, ...)\nsrc = json.dumps(((rec[\"predicate\"].get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}).get(\"time_sources\") or {}))\nself.assertIn(\"harness-eval.log\", src, \"no check time names the harness log as its source\")\n```\n\nHmm, but the emitter's checks come from `passes_src` which is from the \u00a75 record. There's no \u00a75 record in this job. So how can we get a check?\n\nWait \u2014 the bar says: \"the record takes evaluator check times FROM that log\". The D4 test builds a job with a `passes` entry in `inputs/custody.json` (pass `dim1#p1`, with call `dim1#p1`), and a harness log with entry `{\"call\": \"dim1#p1\", \"sent_at\": ..., \"received_at\": ..., \"request\": {\"url\": ...}, \"response\": {\"model\": ...}}`.\n\nSo the emitter must produce checks from... hmm. Currently checks are built from `passes_src`, which comes from the \u00a75 record's `passes`. Without a \u00a75 record, no passes_src. So no checks.\n\nHold on \u2014 maybe the new module needs to make the emitter able to produce a check from the harness log when there's no \u00a75 record? But the bar says \"the record takes evaluator check times FROM that log\". The intent: the check time comes from the log rather than a hand-entered time.\n\nWait, let me reconsider. Maybe the emitter should build checks from custody inputs' `passes` even without an \u00a75 record? Let me look at the tests more carefully.\n\nActually, let's reconsider. The task says the failing tests are D4 and D8. D8 is about reversed times refusal. D4 requires a check whose time_source names harness-eval.log.\n\nFor D4, the emitter must produce at least one check. The job's custody.json has `passes: {\"dim1#p1\": {...}}`. The current emitter builds `checks` from `passes_src` (from \u00a75 record passes). Since there's no \u00a75 record, checks is empty.\n\nHmm, but the bar says the two failures are \"the capability\". So the fix should make the emitter produce checks in this scenario. But is that within scope? The scope is:\n- create `kit/evaluator_harness_log.py` \u2014 \"the module that gives the emitter one reading of a harness log\"\n- edit `kit/emit_custody.py` \u2014 \"use it, and refuse instead of noting\"\n\nLet me look at the D4 test again:\n\n```python\ndef test_d4_record_check_time_comes_from_the_log(self):\n    \"\"\"D4: the record's check time names the harness log as its source.\"\"\"\n    job = self._job(json.dumps(self.GOOD) + \"\\n\")\n    r = self._emit(job)\n    rec = self._record(job)\n    self.assertIsNotNone(rec, f\"no record written\\n{r.stdout}{r.stderr}\")\n    checks = (rec.get(\"predicate\") or {}).get(\"checks\") or []\n    self.assertTrue(checks, f\"no check recorded\\n{r.stdout}{r.stderr}\")\n    src = json.dumps(((rec[\"predicate\"].get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}).get(\"time_sources\") or {}))\n    self.assertIn(\"harness-eval.log\", src, \"no check time names the harness log as its source\")\n```\n\nThe `_record(job)` reads `job / \"custody\" / \"record.custody.json\"`. Note that the emitter refuses if `ref` is non-empty (exit 3, nothing written). But `self.assertIsNotNone(rec)` \u2014 so the record must be written, meaning `ref` must be empty (no refusals). Wait, but also exit code could be 1 if hard gaps. The test doesn't check returncode for D4. But `_record` must exist.\n\nSo for D4 to pass:\n- The emitter must write the record (not refuse).\n- The record must contain at least one check.\n- The record's `x-plumbline.time_sources` must include something with \"harness-eval.log\".\n\nNow, what sources of hard gaps exist in this job that would cause the record to still be written? Hard gaps cause exit 1 but record is still written. So OK, record written even with hard gaps. But `ref` (Refusals) cause exit 3 and NOTHING written. So we must not add refusals for this job.\n\nLet's trace current refusals for D4's job:\n- `H.revision(HERE, job, ...)` \u2014 checks emitter tree is dirty or not stated revision. The repo is a git repo. If the tree is dirty (we're editing files), `H.revision` may add a refusal! Hmm. But the tests presumably currently produce a record for D8 (\"the emitter writes a record anyway\"). So the revision check must be passing in this environment. OK.\n- `H.check_approval` for the buyer approval. The custody.json has no `bar.approvals`, so no approvals loop. But the ledger has an approve buyer line. Hmm, `relay_only_buyer` checks `packet.get(\"buyer\")` \u2014 packet has no buyer, so returns False.\n- F1f relay-only: returns False.\n- maker: `m = ci.get(\"maker\") or {}` \u2192 `{}`. `m.get(\"kind\") == \"model\"` \u2192 False, so `mk = {}`. No maker history, no refusals.\n- No `ci.get(\"startedAt\")`, no producedAt.\n- evaluators: one evaluator with kind \"model\". `evaluator_history(...)`: `rel = e.get(\"harness_log\")` = \"custody/evidence/harness-eval.log\". `find_log(job, ev_dir, rel, None)`: ev_dir = job/custody/evidence, so `(ev_dir/rel)` = `job/custody/evidence/custody/evidence/harness-eval.log` \u2014 doesn't exist. Then `(job/rel)` = `job/custody/evidence/harness-eval.log` \u2014 exists! So log found.\n\nThen `H.read_log(log, ref, who)`. This is in `kit/custody_history.py` which is read-only and I don't have its contents. Hmm. I need to understand its interface. Let me think about what `read_log` does \u2014 presumably reads the log (JSON list) and returns call objects. It may add refusals for malformed logs etc. But I don't have the file. Let me check the summary: it wasn't listed in the summaries. Hmm.\n\nWait, the user gave me `kit/evaluator_harness_log.py` (empty) and `kit/emit_custody.py`. They didn't give `kit/custody_history.py`. But `emit_custody.py` imports it as `H` and uses `H.read_log`, `H.cross_check`, `H.iso`, `H.parse_ts`, `H.Refusals`, `H.revision`, `H.check_approval`, `H.endpoint_of`, `H.model_matches`, `H.routing_problems`, `H.HOST`, `H.AGGREGATORS`, `H.TOLERANCE_S`, and Call attributes `.label`, `.at`, `.started`, `.endpoint`, `.route`, `.model`, `.name`, `.i`, `.raw`, `.sent`, `.received`, `.created`, `.at_basis`, `.source_at()`, `.source_started()`, `.host`, `.routing`, `.hand_time_entries()`.\n\nSince I can't see `custody_history.py`, I must be careful. But the task says I only edit two files. The new module `kit/evaluator_harness_log.py` should give the emitter \"one reading of a harness log\". Maybe it should build on `H.read_log`? Let me think about what's needed.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole approach. Maybe the new module is meant to be used by the emitter to read harness logs, producing checks. Let me look at what the tests need exactly:\n\nD4: record has a check with time source naming harness-eval.log.\nD5: record names \"harness-eval.log\" somewhere (just `json.dumps(record)` contains it).\nD6: missing log \u2192 refuse (exit != 0) and stderr/stdout contains \"harness log\".\nD7: missing log does not degrade to note matching regex `note\\s+external:?\\s*no harness log`.\nD8: reversed times \u2192 refuse (exit != 0), output names \"dim1#p1\".\nD9: partial (no received_at) \u2192 refuse, names \"dim1#p1\".\nD10: malformed log \u2192 refuse.\nD11: deterministic evaluator (kind \"command\") with no log \u2192 not refused with \"needs its harness log\". Wait, D11 asserts `\"needs its harness log\"` not in output. Hmm, where would that string come from? Currently `evaluator_history` adds refusal \"a model evaluator needs its harness log ...\". For kind \"command\", `e.get(\"kind\") == \"model\"` is False, so evaluator_history isn't called. So no refusal. D11's assert is `assertNotIn(\"needs its harness log\", ...)`. The current message is \"needs its harness log\" \u2014 matches. So D11 currently passes (since deterministic evaluator doesn't call evaluator_history, no refusal). Good.\n\nBut wait, D11's job has `evaluator_kind=\"command\"`. The evaluator block still has `harness_log` set, `model` set. The emitter: `e.get(\"kind\") == \"model\"` false so no evaluator_history. The evaluator gets `model` block only if kind model; else `model: None`. And `script` only if kind script. Fine.\n\nNow, D6: `(job / \"custody\" / \"evidence\" / \"harness-eval.log\").unlink()` then emit. Must refuse naming \"harness log\". Currently: `evaluator_history` calls `find_log` \u2192 returns None (file deleted), then `ref.add(\"time\", f\"{who}: a model evaluator needs its harness log ...\")`. So output contains \"harness log\". Exit code 3 (refusal) \u2192 not 0. So D6 should pass currently? The task says only D4 and D8 fail. Let me check D6.\n\nHmm, wait. The refusal message: \"evaluator evaluator: a model evaluator needs its harness log (evaluators[].harness_log, or the CL1-15 external entry for it); not found: 'custody/evidence/harness-eval.log', so its check times and endpoint have no source\". Contains \"harness log\". Exit 3. So D6 passes.\n\nBut D8 (reversed times): the log has one entry with sent_at after received_at. Let's see what happens. `evaluator_history`: log found, `H.read_log(log, ref, who)`. What does read_log do with reversed times? Unknown without the file. Then `calls = [c for c in log_calls if c.at]`. Then `annotate`. Then `check_pin_order`. Then `first = min(calls, key=lambda c: c.at)`. Then endpoint check.\n\nThen back in `build`, for passes: `passes_src` is empty (no \u00a75 record). So the pass `dim1#p1` in `ci[\"passes\"]` is never used! Because checks are only built from `passes_src`. So the `link_call` is never invoked. So no refusal for reversed times.\n\nWait, but why does the task say D8 currently \"writes a record anyway and says note external: no harness log (CL1-15) for model evaluator\"? Because evaluator is model, and external list is empty, so it adds `gaps.add(\"external\", ...)` non-hard. And the checks are empty. And `H.read_log` presumably doesn't refuse reversed times (or maybe it does?). Hmm. Actually the task says D8 currently writes the record. So read_log must NOT refuse reversed times currently. Or maybe it does something else.\n\nHmm, I really need `custody_history.py`. Let me check if there's a way to infer. Actually, wait \u2014 the summary lists didn't include kit/custody_history.py, but maybe it exists. The user said \"Here are summaries of some files present in my git repository\" \u2014 it's a partial list. The file likely exists. I could ask for it, but maybe I can design the new module to do its own log reading, independent of `H.read_log`, and use it in the emitter. But the emitter currently uses `H.read_log` within `evaluator_history`/`maker_history`. I can change those to use the new module.\n\nLet me think about what design satisfies all tests, while being principled.\n\nCore insight: the bar wants the check times to come from the harness log. The job's custody.json declares `passes: {\"dim1#p1\": {\"call\": \"dim1#p1\", ...}}`. But the emitter only builds checks from a \u00a75 record's passes. The bar's job has no \u00a75 record. So maybe the intended change is: when there's no \u00a75 record but the custody inputs declare passes, build checks from those passes (with times taken from the harness log). Hmm, but that contradicts the emitter docstring \"checks: one per (filed pass, bar dimension), from the final iteration's passes\".\n\nWait. Let me re-read the test setup. Actually maybe the `passes` in custody.json is enough. Let's think about the emitter's philosophy: \"It never fabricates. Every digest is computed here from a file that exists; a fact Plumbline has no source for is left null/absent\". Checks from `ci[\"passes\"]` \u2014 the pass facts are given by the Orchestrator's le