attach entries even when calls empty.\n\nLet me write the new `evaluator_history` carefully.\n\nCurrent code:\n\n```python\ndef evaluator_history(job: Path, ev_dir: Path, ci: dict, e: dict, ref: H.Refusals, pin: dict | None = None,\n                      gaps: Gaps | None = None, hand: dict | None = None) -> dict:\n    who = f\"evaluator {e.get('id')}\"\n    rel = e.get(\"harness_log\") or next((x.get(\"evidence_file\") for x in ci.get(\"external\") or []\n                                        if x.get(\"subject\") == e.get(\"id\")), None)\n    log = find_log(job, ev_dir, rel, None)\n    if log is None:\n        ref.add(\"time\", f\"{who}: a model evaluator needs its harness log (evaluators[].harness_log, or the CL1-15 \"\n                        f\"external entry for it); {'not found: ' + repr(rel) if rel else 'none named'}, so its check \"\n                        f\"times and endpoint have no source\")\n        return {}\n    # The emitter never writes its inputs (T7): the log is read as it is. Every call counts for T7b, not only the\n    # call a check is linked to.\n    log_calls = H.read_log(log, ref, who)\n    flag_calls(log_calls, hand)\n    calls = [c for c in log_calls if c.at]\n    if not calls:\n        return {}\n    annotate(calls, who, (e.get(\"model\") or {}).get(\"identifier\"), ref, pin)\n    check_pin_order(pin, calls, who, ref)\n    first = min(calls, key=lambda c: c.at)\n    hand_ep = (e.get(\"model\") or {}).get(\"endpoint\")\n    if hand_ep and first.endpoint and hand_ep != first.endpoint:\n        ref.add(\"endpoint\", f\"evaluators[{e.get('id')}].model.endpoint: hand-entered {hand_ep!r} but {first.label} \"\n                            + (f\"went to {first.host} and was answered upstream by \"\n                               f\"{first.route.get('upstream_provider')!r} ({first.endpoint})\"\n                               if first.route.get(\"aggregator\") else f\"was answered by {first.endpoint}\"))\n    named = {}\n    for c in calls:\n        named.setdefault(c.name or str(c.i), c)\n    x = route_x(log, calls)\n    rx = routing_x(calls, pin, str(e.get(\"id\")), gaps if gaps is not None else Gaps())\n    if rx:\n        x[\"routing\"] = rx\n    return {\"calls\": named, \"endpoint\": first.endpoint, \"x\": x}\n```\n\nI'll insert after `log = find_log(...)` block:\n\n```python\n    # ONE reading of the log (kit/evaluator_harness_log.py) BEFORE any call is linked to a check: a malformed,\n    # partial or reversed entry is refused here, naming the entry, so no check time is taken from a log the\n    # record cannot honestly read. The existing per-call reading below still supplies endpoints and routes.\n    try:\n        entries = harness_log.read(log)\n    except harness_log.HarnessLogError as exc:\n        ref.add(\"time\", f\"{who}: {exc}\")\n        return {}\n```\n\nThen at the end, include `\"entries\": entries`. And for the early `if not calls: return {}`, change to `return {\"entries\": entries, \"calls\": {}, \"endpoint\": None, \"x\": route_x(log, log_calls)}`. Hmm, but route_x expects calls; with empty list it returns `{\"harness_log\": log.name, \"calls\": []}`. Fine.\n\nActually, if `calls` is empty but entries exist, we still want the check time from entries. So return entries.\n\nLet me modify `if not calls:` block:\n\n```python\n    if not calls:\n        return {\"entries\": entries, \"calls\": {},\n                \"endpoint\": None, \"x\": {\"harness_log\": log.name, \"calls\": []}}\n```\n\nNow the end:\n\n```python\n    return {\"calls\": named, \"endpoint\": first.endpoint, \"x\": x, \"entries\": entries}\n```\n\nNow, in `build`, capture `ev_entries`:\n\n```python\n    evs, ev_calls, ev_ep = [], {}, {}\n```\n\u2192\n```python\n    evs, ev_calls, ev_ep, ev_entries = [], {}, {}, {}\n```\n\nand inside:\n\n```python\n        if e.get(\"kind\") == \"model\":\n            eh = evaluator_history(...)\n            ev_calls[e.get(\"id\")], ev_ep[e.get(\"id\")] = eh.get(\"calls\", {}), eh.get(\"endpoint\")\n            ev_entries[e.get(\"id\")] = eh.get(\"entries\") or {}\n```\n\nWait, the existing line is:\n\n```python\n        if e.get(\"kind\") == \"model\":\n            eh = evaluator_history(job, ev_dir, ci, e, ref, pin_for(ci, ev_log, str(e.get(\"id\")), ref), gaps, hand)\n            ev_calls[e.get(\"id\")], ev_ep[e.get(\"id\")] = eh.get(\"calls\", {}), eh.get(\"endpoint\")\n            if eh.get(\"endpoint\"):\n                e_model[\"endpoint\"] = eh[\"endpoint\"]\n```\n\nAdd `ev_entries[e.get(\"id\")] = eh.get(\"entries\") or {}`.\n\nNow the check loop. Current:\n\n```python\n        call = link_call(ev_calls, f.get(\"evaluator\"), f.get(\"call\"),\n                         \"eval_artifact\" if n_passes == 1 else None, f\"passes.{pid}\", ref)\n        at_v, ep_v, xc = f.get(\"at\"), f.get(\"endpoint\"), {}\n        if call is not None:\n            H.cross_check(ref, f\"passes.{pid}.at\", f.get(\"at\"), call.at, f\"harness log {call.label}\")\n            at_v, xc = H.iso(call.at), {\"call\": call.label, \"at_basis\": call.at_basis}\n            if call.source_at():\n                xc[\"at_source\"] = call.source_at()\n            if f.get(\"endpoint\") and call.endpoint and f[\"endpoint\"] != call.endpoint:\n                ref.add(\"endpoint\", f\"passes.{pid}.endpoint: hand-entered {f['endpoint']!r} but {call.label} was \"\n                                    f\"answered by {call.endpoint}\")\n            ep_v = call.endpoint if call.endpoint and call.endpoint != ev_ep.get(f.get(\"evaluator\")) else None\n        elif f.get(\"at\"):\n            n = line_in(inputs_path, f.get(\"at\"), \"at\")\n            if n:\n                xc = {\"at_source\": f\"{rel_inputs}:{n}\"}\n```\n\nInsert after the `if/elif`:\n\n```python\n        # The check's time comes FROM the harness log: the module named the entry (`<log>:<line>`), so a reader\n        # can find the call the time was read from. This holds whether or not the per-call reader linked it.\n        entry = (ev_entries.get(f.get(\"evaluator\")) or {}).get(f.get(\"call\"))\n        if entry is not None:\n            at_v = H.iso(entry.received_at)\n            xc[\"at_source\"] = entry.source\n            xc.setdefault(\"call\", entry.name)\n```\n\nThen the dim loop uses `at_v` and `xc`.\n\nWait, but there's a subtlety: if `call is not None` but `f.get(\"at\")` is a hand time that differs from `call.at`, `H.cross_check` adds a refusal. For D4, `f.get(\"at\")` is None, so no refusal. Good.\n\nNow, the source: `entry.source` should be e.g. \"harness-eval.log:1\". Let me implement `Entry.source` to include the log name.\n\nBut careful: `H.iso(entry.received_at)` \u2014 `entry.received_at` is a datetime. `H.iso` presumably formats with Z. Good.\n\nNow let me also double-check `ts(at_v, ...)` uses `at_v` (now a string). `ts` validates RFC. `H.iso` returns RFC. Good.\n\nNow D4: `checks` will have one entry. `x-plumbline.time_sources` includes `checks[0].at` = \"harness-eval.log:1\". Wait, `time_sources` uses `(c.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}).get(\"at_source\")`. In the check dict, `c[\"x-plumbline\"] = x` where `x = {\"pass_id\": pid, **xc}`. `xc` has `at_source`. So `x[\"at_source\"] = entry.source`. Good.\n\nActually, let me re-check the check dict construction:\n\n```python\n            x = {\"pass_id\": pid, **xc}\n            if x.get(\"at_source\"):\n                xp[\"sources\"][f\"checks[{pid}/{dim}].at\"] = x[\"at_source\"]\n```\n\nGood. And `time_sources(pred, xp)` will pick it up again from `c.get(\"x-plumbline\")`.\n\nNow, there's also `for i, c in enumerate(ci.get(\"checks\") or [])` \u2014 empty.\n\nNow, `pfacts` fallback: I need to make sure `passes_src` is defined. Currently:\n\n```python\n    rec_path, rec = final_record(job)\n    passes_src: list[dict] = []\n    run = None\n    if rec:\n        ...\n        for pn in rec.get(\"passes\") or []:\n            pf = ...\n            passes_src.append(...)\n        run = run_for(...)\n    else:\n        xp[\"verdict\"] = ci.get(\"verdict\")\n        if xp[\"verdict\"] is None:\n            gaps.add(\"x-plumbline.verdict\", ...)\n```\n\nI'll add in the else:\n\n```python\n    else:\n        xp[\"verdict\"] = ci.get(\"verdict\")\n        if xp[\"verdict\"] is None:\n            gaps.add(\"x-plumbline.verdict\", \"no \u00a75 record in the job and no verdict in the custody inputs\", False)\n        # A job with no \u00a75 record still declares its passes in the custody inputs; build the checks from those\n        # passes so their times can come from the harness log (D4) instead of being left unrecorded.\n        passes_src = [{\"pass_id\": pid} for pid in (ci.get(\"passes\") or {})]\n```\n\nGood.\n\nHmm wait, but `run` is used for `quotes` extraction. `run=None` so quotes empty. Fine.\n\nNow, let me also consider: `n_passes = sum(1 for q in pfacts.values() if q.get(\"evaluator\") == f.get(\"evaluator\"))` = 1. `\"eval_artifact\" if n_passes == 1 else None`. `link_call(..., named=f.get(\"call\")=\"dim1#p1\", default=\"eval_artifact\", ...)`. If `ev_calls[\"evaluator\"]` has \"dim1#p1\" \u2192 returns. If not, tries default \"eval_artifact\" if in calls; else None; and since `named` is not None, no single-call fallback. It may add refusal \"no harness call ... linked\". Wait:\n\n```python\n    if name not in calls:\n        ref.add(\"time\", f\"{where}: no harness call of evaluator {ev_id} is linked to it \"\n                        ...)\n        return None\n```\n\nSo if `named` (\"dim1#p1\") is not in `calls`, it adds a REFUSAL. That would break D4 if `H.read_log` doesn't name calls correctly! Hmm.\n\nSo D4 hinges on `H.read_log` keying the call by \"dim1#p1\". If not, `link_call` adds a refusal \u2192 exit 3 \u2192 no record \u2192 D4 fails.\n\nTo be safe, I could make `link_call` not refuse when the module has the entry. Hmm. But `link_call` is shared with controls.\n\nAlternative: build `ev_calls` from my module entries as well, so link_call finds them. But