\"call\")` in ev_map, so name found. Fine.\n\nIf `f.get(\"call\")` absent and `ev_map` non-empty, linkable True, link_call with named None \u2192 picks default or single. Might refuse if ambiguous. Existing behavior. For our fixture `f.get(\"call\")` present. Fine.\n\nOK. Now let me also verify D4's `time_sources` test path. `time_sources(pred, xp)`:\n\n```python\n    for i, c in enumerate(pred.get(\"checks\") or []):\n        s = (c.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}).get(\"at_source\")\n        if s:\n            out[f\"checks[{i}].at\"] = s\n```\n\nOur check's `x-plumbline` is `x = {\"pass_id\": pid, **xc}`. `xc[\"at_source\"] = entry.source` = \"harness-eval.log:1\". So `out[\"checks[0].at\"] = \"harness-eval.log:1\"`. `json.dumps(...)` contains \"harness-eval.log\". D4 passes.\n\nNow, let me make sure `entry.source` isn't None. `_line_of` finds line 1. `received_line=1`. `source=\"harness-eval.log:1\"`. Good.\n\nNow, let's double check that we don't accidentally get a refusal from `H.cross_check` if `call` is linked and `f.get(\"at\")` is None. Should be fine.\n\nAlso, the `annotate` and `check_pin_order` in evaluator_history might add refusals? `pin` is None (no routing in ci). `annotate(calls, who, identifier, ref, pin=None)`: for each call, `H.endpoint_of(c, ref, who, pin)`. The GOOD entry has `request.url = \"https://api.z.ai/chat/completions\"`. `endpoint_of` might parse. Since pin None, direct. Probably no refusal. `H.model_matches(c.model, \"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\")` \u2014 c.model from `response.model` = \"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\". Matches. Good.\n\nBut wait: does `H.read_log` extract `c.model` from `response.model`? The fixture's response is `{\"model\": \"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\"}`. If `H.read_log`'s Call takes model from `request.body.model` (or_call writes model in request body, not response). The fixture has no request body model; only response.model. So `c.model` might be None \u2192 `model_matches(None, identifier)` \u2014 might add a refusal \"ran model None, not 