et me re-scan the refused() calls with LOGGED base for causes that might vanish... Their causes are all in inputs/logs unrelated to logger times. I'm fairly confident.\n\nBut one: `refused(\"a control linked to no call in the harness log\", job_copy(\"unlinked-control\"), \"time\")` \u2713.\n\nAnd `refused(\"a hand time 61 s off its harness call\", j, \"time\")` \u2713.\n\nAnd `o = refused(\"a hand vendor host when the log shows the routed upstream\", j, \"endpoint\")` \u2713.\n\nHmm, one thing: `j = job_copy(\"pin-attempt\")` then `lg = ...; x = json.loads(lg.read_text())` \u2014 LOGGED's maker log preserved as a dict \u2713 (my `_stamp_logger_times` writes back the same form for dict). Ensure the dict branch writes the whole dict back with indent=2 (format change is fine since json.loads works).\n\nCareful: if the maker log is a dict, `_server_instant(e)` where e = the dict itself (items=[doc]) \u2014 a single call object with \"response\" \u2713.\n\nBut what if the file is a dict wrapper like `{\"calls\": [...]}`? Then we'd try to stamp the wrapper and no calls get sent_at \u2192 fix fails (refusal persists). The other tests (`x[\"response\"][\"openrouter_metadata\"]`) prove the top-level dict IS a call \u2713.\n\nAnd `harness-eval-a.log`: list or JSONL with \u22653 entries \u2713.\n\nHmm, what about `same-family`: it does `ml.read_text().replace(\"fixture/maker-1\", \"example-1\")` \u2014 on the dict form \u2713.\n\nNow let's also double check `logger_stamped` copies FIX \u2192 LOGGED created once; but `job_copy` copies LOGGED \u2192 each job has fresh copies \u2713 and jobs that MODIFY logs don't affect LOGGED \u2713.\n\nOne catch: `same-family` writes `ml` in the job copy \u2713.\n\nAnother catch: `clean_checkout`/SNAP unaffected.\n\nNow about `rec` used later for the \"matching pin\" checks: `mx = rec[\"predicate\"][\"maker\"]` \u2713 from LOGGED record; maker endpoint \"api.deepinfra.com\" \u2713 (log unchanged in endpoint terms... wait, we stamped times only \u2713).\n\nHmm, `mxx.get(\"routing\").get(\"request_ok\")` \u2014 from LOGGED's maker log (unchanged request) \u2713.\n\nNow \u2014 a possible issue with LOGGED: `x-plumbline.times` = {\"startedAt\": \"harness log\", ...} now, affecting `check_order`'s tolerance (logged events get tolerance) \u2014 previously hand-entered \u2192 strict. With LOGGED, times equal a close date? The fixture has no close (packet close popped only in tool_built_job). Does FIX's packet.json have a `close.date`? If yes and startedAt == producedAt == log times, and close date is later \u2713 fine. Tolerance only loosens \u2713.\n\nAnother: `after-emit` check in check_order: `t > now + tol`. The fixture's times are 2026-10-20 \u2192 in the past \u2713.\n\nOK, now also: does `emit(LOGGED, ...)` produce `x-plumbline.hand_times` containing maker/evaluator entries? No (all logged) \u2014 only typed ones (approvals, disposition). For T3 `len(ht) >= 1` \u2713.\n\nHmm, but T3 also asserts `by_field[\"disposition.at\"].get(\"line\") is not None` \u2014 depends on `line_in(inputs_path, at, \"at\")` finding the line in custody.json \u2713 (typed there).\n\nWait, actually: is disposition.at typed in FIX's custody.json? T2c asserts disposition.at is named as inputs-no-ledger \u2713 yes.\n\nNow: E1 dispose-mismatch is `job_copy(\"dispose-mismatch\")` \u2192 LOGGED base; appends a dispose line with decided_at 12:31 while custody.json has at 12:30 \u2192 [time] \u2713.\n\nHmm, but with LOGGED, the record... refusal anyway \u2713.\n\nNow consider \"live-match\": appends matching freeze+approve lines \u2192 expects rc 0 and `rl[\"bar\"][\"approvals\"][1][\"x-plumbline\"][\"time_source\"].startswith(\"logged live\")` \u2713.\n\n\"agent-adopted\" rc 0 \u2713.\n\n\"f1h\": rc 0 \u2713 \u2014 but wait, it appends ledger lines with `writer: kit/custody_ledger.py@...` and times 2026-10-20T10:xx. `check_order` may now complain about order? The times are 10:30/10:32 etc. vs check times 12:00 \u2713.\n\nHmm, and `sp